  "description": "The person definition identified by\u202fhttps://example.com/schemas/person.schema.json (conforming to the Draft\u201107 meta\u2011schema at\u202fhttp://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#) is an object titled \u201cPerson\u201d and described as \u201cA schema defining a person object.\u201d  Every instance must be an object (not\u202fnull) whose property names are non\u2011empty strings, and no properties other than those explicitly listed are permitted.  Required top\u2011level members are\u202fname\u202f(a string of length\u202f1\u202fto\u202f100 characters) and\u202fage\u202f(an integer\u202f\u2265\u202f0).  In addition, the schema enforces that an\u202femail\u202ffield must be present, must follow the email format, and must match the regular expression\u202f`^[^@\\s]+@[^@\\s]+\\.[^@\\s]+$`.  Any property whose key begins with the prefix\u202f\u201cS_\u201d must be a string.  All other optional members are limited to\u202faddress,\u202femail,\u202fcredit_card\u202fand\u202fbilling_address\u202fas described below, and the object as a whole may not be null.\n\nThe optional\u202faddress\u202fmember is defined by the reusable \u201caddress\u201d definition: it is an object containing the required string fields\u202fstreet,\u202fcity, and\u202fpostalCode, the latter constrained by the pattern\u202f`^[0-9]{5}$` (exactly five digits), and it disallows additional properties.  The reusable \u201cpositiveNumber\u201d definition declares a number with a minimum value of\u202f0; this is applied to the\u202fcredit_card\u202fproperty, which therefore must be a non\u2011negative number.  The schema also specifies a dependency: the presence of\u202fbilling_address\u202frequires that\u202fcredit_card\u202fbe present as well.  According to the\u202fallOf\u202fclause, the object must include an\u202femail\u202ffield and the\u202fage\u202fvalue must respect its non\u2011negative minimum.  The\u202fanyOf\u202fclause states that an instance must contain either a\u202fname\u202for an\u202faddress\u202ffield, while the\u202foneOf\u202fclause requires that exactly one of the following be satisfied: the object includes an\u202femail\u202ffield or it includes an\u202fage\u202ffield.  By default, an empty object (`{}`) is used as the base value, and any attempt to add unspecified properties will be rejected."
